       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is twice the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Higher doses mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 20 mg PO once daily as written.** This is for an intentional off-label dose. If you choose it, please confirm that it's intended, and I'll add a note to the order saying it's above the usual maximum.\n3. **Something else**, such as 10 mg plus a second agent (an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide-like diuretic) if blood pressure is still uncontrolled.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it."
      }
